---
import ServicePage from '../../components/services/ServicePage.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const canonical = 'https://busqueneil.com/hire/ai-engineer-remote';

const FAQ = [
  {
    q: 'How do we stay in touch?',
    a: 'WhatsApp or email day to day, with a link to try after each round, and a call when a decision is easier to make together. I reply myself, usually the same day.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which time zone do you work in?',
    a: 'US Eastern. That overlaps with every US time zone and part of the European afternoon, and still leaves uninterrupted time to build.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who owns the code?',
    a: 'You do. The code and the accounts it runs on are in your name. If we ever stop working together, everything stays with you.',
  },
];
---
<ServicePage
  title="Remote AI Engineer in US Eastern Time | Neil Busque"
  description="Neil Busque is a remote AI engineer building agents, automations and web apps from the US East Coast, with clear updates and frequent preview links."
  canonical={canonical}
  active="hire"
  heading="Hire a **remote AI engineer**."
  lead="I build AI agents, automations and web apps remotely from the US East Coast. You get written updates, frequent preview links and calls when a decision is easier to make together."
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/' },
    { name: 'Hire', url: 'https://busqueneil.com/hire' },
    { name: 'Remote AI Engineer', url: canonical },
  ]}
  backLabel="When to hire me"
  topic="hiring a remote AI engineer"
  artSeed="hire-ai-engineer-remote"
  artPalette="mist"
  summary={{
    items: [
      'Written updates in plain English',
      'Preview links as the build takes shape',
      'Calls when a decision is easier together',
      'AI agents, automations and web apps',
      'The code and the accounts, in your name',
    ],
    facts: [
      { term: 'Good for', value: 'Teams anywhere in the US, and some in Europe' },
      { term: 'How it starts', value: 'A message on WhatsApp or email' },
      { term: 'What you own', value: 'The code, the data and every account' },
    ],
  }}
  related={['crm-with-ai-follow-up', 'funnel-simulator']}
  relatedPalettes={['mist', 'navy']}
  faq={FAQ}
  service={{
    name: 'Remote AI Engineer',
    serviceType: ['Remote AI engineering', 'AI agent development', 'AI automation', 'Web app development'],
    areaServed: [{ '@type': 'Country', name: 'United States' }, 'Remote', 'Worldwide'],
  }}
>
  <h2>Remote that actually works</h2>
  <p>Remote work goes wrong when the project disappears for a month. I keep the tasks small, ship often and share preview links as the build takes shape. You review real progress instead of reading a status paragraph.</p>

  <h2>A time zone that overlaps</h2>
  <p>I work on US Eastern time. That gives working overlap with every US time zone and part of the European afternoon, while leaving enough uninterrupted time to build.</p>

  <h2>What I ship remotely</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>AI agents</strong> wired into your tools. See <a href="/guides/build-ai-agent-claude-code">how I build them</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Automations</strong> that remove manual work in n8n, Zapier and GoHighLevel.</li>
    <li><strong>Web apps</strong> with a working first version in days. Here is <a href="/guides/ship-web-app-in-days-with-ai">the process</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>GEO and SEO</strong> so you get found in AI search. See <a href="/guides/geo-generative-engine-optimization-guide">the GEO guide</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Hire me remotely</h2>
  <p>Message me on WhatsApp, email <a href="mailto:busqueneil@gmail.com">busqueneil@gmail.com</a> or connect on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/neilbusque/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>. Prefer someone local to the NYC area? See <a href="/hire/ai-engineer-nj">New Jersey</a> or <a href="/hire/ai-engineer-nyc">NYC</a>. More on <a href="/hire">when to bring me in</a>.</p>
</ServicePage>
